Key objectives include enhancing transparency, fostering investor confidence, and aligning Swedish corporate practices with international standards. The law encourages sustainable development by emphasizing ESG criteria, supporting Sweden’s environmental and social goals.', 'Sweden', 'climate', 'in_force', '1995-01-01'::date, 'Sweden', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/171_100', ARRAY['sdg13', 'sdg10', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'sweden']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('ce9fea6a-b510-5c23-adaf-2c106aff348b', 'Switzerland Federal Act on the Amendment of the Swiss', 'Federal Act on the Amendment of the Swiss Civil Code (Part Five: The Code of Obligations)', 'The Federal Act on the Amendment of the Swiss Civil Code (Part Five: The Code of Obligations) is a legislative update that governs contracts, obligations, and corporate governance within Switzerland. The amendments aim to enhance transparency, accountability, and sustainability in corporate practices, reflecting global trends in responsible business conduct. It also aligns Switzerland’s corporate framework with international sustainability and human rights standards.

Key elements include:

Enhanced Non-Financial Reporting:

Large public companies and financial institutions must disclose non-financial information, including environmental, social, and governance (ESG) factors.

Reporting requirements align with frameworks such as GRI and TCFD.

Human Rights and Environmental Due Diligence:

Companies must identify and address human rights risks and environmental impacts in their value chains.

Specific obligations for businesses operating in high-risk sectors or regions.

Corporate Governance Improvements:

Enhanced shareholder rights and transparency in executive compensation.

Mandatory sustainability-related disclosures in annual reports.

This act strengthens Switzerland’s legal alignment with global frameworks, including the OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises and the UN Guiding Principles on Business and Human Rights.', 'The Federal Act on the Amendment of the Swiss Civil Code (Part Five: The Code of Obligations) is a legislative update that governs contracts, obligations, and corporate governance within Switzerland. The amendments aim to enhance transparency, accountability, and sustainability in corporate practices, reflecting global trends in responsible business conduct. It also aligns Switzerland’s corporate framework with international sustainability and human rights standards.

Key elements include:

Enhanced Non-Financial Reporting:

Large public companies and financial institutions must disclose non-financial information, including environmental, social, and governance (ESG) factors.

Reporting requirements align with frameworks such as GRI and TCFD.

Human Rights and Environmental Due Diligence:

Companies must identify and address human rights risks and environmental impacts in their value chains.

Specific obligations for businesses operating in high-risk sectors or regions.

Corporate Governance Improvements:

Enhanced shareholder rights and transparency in executive compensation.

Mandatory sustainability-related disclosures in annual reports.

This act strengthens Switzerland’s legal alignment with global frameworks, including the OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises and the UN Guiding Principles on Business and Human Rights.', 'The Federal Act on the Amendment of the Swiss Civil Code (Part Five: The Code of Obligations) is a legislative update that governs contracts, obligations, and corporate governance within Switzerland. The amendments aim to enhance transparency, accountability, and sustainability in corporate practices, reflecting global trends in responsible business conduct. It also aligns Switzerland’s corporate framework with international sustainability and human rights standards.

Key elements include:

Enhanced Non-Financial Reporting:

Large public companies and financial institutions must disclose non-financial information, including environmental, social, and governance (ESG) factors.

Reporting requirements align with frameworks such as GRI and TCFD.

Human Rights and Environmental Due Diligence:

Companies must identify and address human rights risks and environmental impacts in their value chains.

Specific obligations for businesses operating in high-risk sectors or regions.

Corporate Governance Improvements:

Enhanced shareholder rights and transparency in executive compensation.

Mandatory sustainability-related disclosures in annual reports.

This act strengthens Switzerland’s legal alignment with global frameworks, including the OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises and the UN Guiding Principles on Business and Human Rights.', 'Switzerland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2025-01-01'::date, 'Switzerland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/172_1', ARRAY['regulations', 'sdg9', 'mandatory', 'switzerland', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'sdg15', 'sdg3']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('7864dd23-18b3-593d-8cdb-698ef5a33ff6', 'Switzerland Federal Act of 23 December 2011 on the', 'Federal Act of 23 December 2011 on the Reduction of CO2 Emissions (CO2 Act)', 'The Swiss Federal Act of 2011 on CO2 Emissions Reduction aims to implement climate goals set in a prior law. It establishes emission reduction targets, outlines key terms like fossil fuels and emission rights, and encourages voluntary emission reduction measures. The policy targets various sectors for reducing CO2 emissions by at least 35% by 2030 compared to 1990 levels.', 'The Swiss Federal Act of 2011 on CO2 Emissions Reduction aims to implement climate goals set in a prior law. It establishes emission reduction targets, outlines key terms like fossil fuels and emission rights, and encourages voluntary emission reduction measures. The policy targets various sectors for reducing CO2 emissions by at least 35% by 2030 compared to 1990 levels.', 'The Swiss Federal Act of 2011 on CO2 Emissions Reduction aims to implement climate goals set in a prior law. It establishes emission reduction targets, outlines key terms like fossil fuels and emission rights, and encourages voluntary emission reduction measures. The policy targets various sectors for reducing CO2 emissions by at least 35% by 2030 compared to 1990 levels.', 'Switzerland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2025-01-01'::date, 'Switzerland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/172_37', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'mandatory', 'switzerland', 'sdg15']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('77b3f0a9-7232-54a5-8287-ce71554f5a0e', 'Switzerland Federal Law on Environmental Protection (Environmental Protection Act', 'Federal Law on Environmental Protection (Environmental Protection Act, USG)', 'The Federal Law on Environmental Protection in Switzerland aims to safeguard humans, animals, plants, and ecosystems from harmful impacts. It emphasizes cost responsibility for those causing environmental harm and sets standards for emissions, waste management, and protection of natural resources. Targeted at individuals, businesses, and government agencies.', 'The Federal Law on Environmental Protection in Switzerland aims to safeguard humans, animals, plants, and ecosystems from harmful impacts. It emphasizes cost responsibility for those causing environmental harm and sets standards for emissions, waste management, and protection of natural resources. Targeted at individuals, businesses, and government agencies.', 'The Federal Law on Environmental Protection in Switzerland aims to safeguard humans, animals, plants, and ecosystems from harmful impacts. It emphasizes cost responsibility for those causing environmental harm and sets standards for emissions, waste management, and protection of natural resources. Targeted at individuals, businesses, and government agencies.', 'Switzerland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2025-01-01'::date, 'Switzerland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/172_42', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'switzerland', 'sdg12', 'sdg15']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('03fa3140-97ca-5d80-b8a8-eea6f696602b', 'Switzerland Federal law against unfair competition (UWG)', 'Federal law against unfair competition (UWG)', 'The Federal Act on Unfair Competition in Switzerland aims to ensure fair competition by prohibiting misleading practices. It outlines unlawful behaviors in advertising, sales, and consumer credit agreements to protect competitors, suppliers, and customers from deceptive tactics.', 'The Federal Act on Unfair Competition in Switzerland aims to ensure fair competition by prohibiting misleading practices. It outlines unlawful behaviors in advertising, sales, and consumer credit agreements to protect competitors, suppliers, and customers from deceptive tactics.', 'The Federal Act on Unfair Competition in Switzerland aims to ensure fair competition by prohibiting misleading practices. It outlines unlawful behaviors in advertising, sales, and consumer credit agreements to protect competitors, suppliers, and customers from deceptive tactics.', 'Switzerland', 'nature', 'in_force', '2025-01-01'::date, 'Switzerland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/172_43', ARRAY['sdg15', 'mandatory', 'switzerland', 'regulations']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('fbab7f7e-3231-53b2-a8cf-aeccba940605', 'Switzerland Circular 2026/1 Nature-related financial risks Management of climate', 'Circular 2026/1 Nature-related financial risks Management of climate- and other nature-related financial risks', 'Circular 2026/1 from Switzerland outlines the management of climate- and nature-related financial risks for banks and insurers. Effective from 2026, it sets provisions for risk identification, management, and stress tests. The document applies to various financial institutions, emphasizing proportionality and risk integration within conglomerates.', 'Circular 2026/1 from Switzerland outlines the management of climate- and nature-related financial risks for banks and insurers. Effective from 2026, it sets provisions for risk identification, management, and stress tests. The document applies to various financial institutions, emphasizing proportionality and risk integration within conglomerates.', 'Circular 2026/1 from Switzerland outlines the management of climate- and nature-related financial risks for banks and insurers. Effective from 2026, it sets provisions for risk identification, management, and stress tests. The document applies to various financial institutions, emphasizing proportionality and risk integration within conglomerates.', 'Switzerland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2024-01-01'::date, 'Switzerland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/172_38', ARRAY['sdg13', 'mandatory', 'switzerland', 'mandatory_regulations', 'sdg15']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('cf2e650e-b7bb-5224-9c97-cfca72f2732e', 'Switzerland Federal Act on the Reduction of CO2 Emissions', 'Federal Act on the Reduction of CO2 Emissions (CO2 Act)', 'The Federal Act on the Reduction of CO2 Emissions (CO2 Act) in Switzerland, effective 2024, aims to implement climate goals by reducing greenhouse gas emissions. It defines terms, sets reduction targets, and outlines measures for sectors to follow. Target audience includes industries and the government.', 'The Federal Act on the Reduction of CO2 Emissions (CO2 Act) in Switzerland, effective 2024, aims to implement climate goals by reducing greenhouse gas emissions. It defines terms, sets reduction targets, and outlines measures for sectors to follow. Target audience includes industries and the government.', 'The Federal Act on the Reduction of CO2 Emissions (CO2 Act) in Switzerland, effective 2024, aims to implement climate goals by reducing greenhouse gas emissions. It defines terms, sets reduction targets, and outlines measures for sectors to follow. Target audience includes industries and the government.', 'Switzerland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2024-01-01'::date, 'Switzerland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/172_41', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'switzerland', 'sdg15']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('d7eb3de5-65aa-54da-a24e-df4392148b8a', 'Switzerland Information on Corporate Governance', 'Policy regarding Information on Corporate Governance', 'The policy on Information on Corporate Governance in Switzerland, effective from January 2023, outlines disclosure requirements for companies listed on SIX Swiss Exchange. It aims to provide investors with key information on governance practices, emphasizing clarity, relevance, and compliance with international standards.', 'The policy on Information on Corporate Governance in Switzerland, effective from January 2023, outlines disclosure requirements for companies listed on SIX Swiss Exchange. It aims to provide investors with key information on governance practices, emphasizing clarity, relevance, and compliance with international standards.', 'The policy on Information on Corporate Governance in Switzerland, effective from January 2023, outlines disclosure requirements for companies listed on SIX Swiss Exchange. It aims to provide investors with key information on governance practices, emphasizing clarity, relevance, and compliance with international standards.', 'Switzerland', 'nature', 'in_force', '2023-01-01'::date, 'Switzerland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/172_40', ARRAY['mandatory', 'switzerland', 'sdg16', 'mandatory_regulations', 'sdg15']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('779eca06-8f58-5f8a-a1f0-244ad5e9d543', 'Switzerland Climate Disclosures', 'Ordinance on Climate Disclosures', 'The Ordinance on Climate Disclosures, issued by the Swiss Federal Council, establishes mandatory requirements for climate-related disclosures under Articles 964a to 964c of the Swiss Code of Obligations. Effective from 1 January 2024, the ordinance requires companies meeting specific criteria to disclose climate-related information in alignment with the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) recommendations. This aims to enhance transparency, comparability, and accountability in corporate climate reporting, supporting Switzerland’s climate goals.', 'The Ordinance on Climate Disclosures, issued by the Swiss Federal Council, establishes mandatory requirements for climate-related disclosures under Articles 964a to 964c of the Swiss Code of Obligations. Effective from 1 January 2024, the ordinance requires companies meeting specific criteria to disclose climate-related information in alignment with the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) recommendations. This aims to enhance transparency, comparability, and accountability in corporate climate reporting, supporting Switzerland’s climate goals.', 'The Ordinance on Climate Disclosures, issued by the Swiss Federal Council, establishes mandatory requirements for climate-related disclosures under Articles 964a to 964c of the Swiss Code of Obligations. Effective from 1 January 2024, the ordinance requires companies meeting specific criteria to disclose climate-related information in alignment with the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) recommendations. This aims to enhance transparency, comparability, and accountability in corporate climate reporting, supporting Switzerland’s climate goals.', 'Switzerland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2022-01-01'::date, 'Switzerland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/172_2', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'sdg9', 'mandatory', 'switzerland', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'sdg15']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('b7e3783f-1bdd-588e-aec7-514f22e8469d', 'Switzerland Federal Law on Climate Protection Goals, Innovation', 'Federal Law on Climate Protection Goals, Innovation and Strengthening Energy Security (KlG)', 'The Swiss Federal Law on Climate Protection Goals, Innovation, and Energy Security aims to achieve net-zero greenhouse gas emissions by 2050 through emission reductions and negative emission technologies. It sets sector-specific reduction targets, mandates net-zero emissions for all companies by 2050, and provides financial support for innovative technologies.', 'The Swiss Federal Law on Climate Protection Goals, Innovation, and Energy Security aims to achieve net-zero greenhouse gas emissions by 2050 through emission reductions and negative emission technologies. It sets sector-specific reduction targets, mandates net-zero emissions for all companies by 2050, and provides financial support for innovative technologies.', 'The Swiss Federal Law on Climate Protection Goals, Innovation, and Energy Security aims to achieve net-zero greenhouse gas emissions by 2050 through emission reductions and negative emission technologies. It sets sector-specific reduction targets, mandates net-zero emissions for all companies by 2050, and provides financial support for innovative technologies.', 'Switzerland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2022-01-01'::date, 'Switzerland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/172_36', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'sdg9', 'mandatory', 'switzerland', 'sdg15']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('5631a816-4e25-54c3-8e6a-4a6ca7fa4497', 'Switzerland Climate Disclosures, made under the Swiss Code of', 'Ordinance on Climate Disclosures, made under the Swiss Code of Obligations', 'The Ordinance on Climate Disclosures in Switzerland mandates companies to report on climate issues following Task Force recommendations. Requirements include governance, strategy, risk management, and emission disclosures. The policy targets companies to enhance transparency and accountability on climate-related financial matters.', 'The Ordinance on Climate Disclosures in Switzerland mandates companies to report on climate issues following Task Force recommendations. Requirements include governance, strategy, risk management, and emission disclosures. The policy targets companies to enhance transparency and accountability on climate-related financial matters.', 'The Ordinance on Climate Disclosures in Switzerland mandates companies to report on climate issues following Task Force recommendations. Requirements include governance, strategy, risk management, and emission disclosures. The policy targets companies to enhance transparency and accountability on climate-related financial matters.', 'Switzerland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2022-01-01'::date, 'Switzerland', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/172_39', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'switzerland', 'sdg16', 'sdg15']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('e4de12d3-8713-59ce-821d-02c915f6e52f', 'Switzerland Information relating to Corporate Governance', 'Directive on Information relating to Corporate Governance', 'The Directive on Information Relating to Corporate Governance, issued by SIX Exchange Regulation, establishes mandatory disclosure requirements for issuers listed on the SIX Swiss Exchange. The directive ensures transparency, consistency, and accessibility of corporate governance information, enabling investors to make informed decisions. It aligns with the Federal Act on Financial Market Infrastructures and Market Conduct in Securities and Derivatives Trading (FMIA) and incorporates internationally recognized standards.', 'The Directive on Information Relating to Corporate Governance, issued by SIX Exchange Regulation, establishes mandatory disclosure requirements for issuers listed on the SIX Swiss Exchange. The directive ensures transparency, consistency, and accessibility of corporate governance information, enabling investors to make informed decisions. It aligns with the Federal Act on Financial Market Infrastructures and Market Conduct in Securities and Derivatives Trading (FMIA) and incorporates internationally recognized standards.', 'The Directive on Information Relating to Corporate Governance, issued by SIX Exchange Regulation, establishes mandatory disclosure requirements for issuers listed on the SIX Swiss Exchange. The directive ensures transparency, consistency, and accessibility of corporate governance information, enabling investors to make informed decisions. It aligns with the Federal Act on Financial Market Infrastructures and Market Conduct in Securities and Derivatives Trading (FMIA) and incorporates internationally recognized standards.', 'Switzerland', 'climate', 'in_force', '2021-01-01'::date, 'Switzerland', 'http